  "verbalization": "Mitomycin is linked to SQ20B through a series of target relationships, with the most direct pathway involving the enzyme Lysine-specific demethylase 4C. This enzyme is targeted by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which in turn has SQ20B as its target. The second pathway connects mitomycin to TE-9, which also targets the same compound, leading to SQ20B. While the exact mechanism by which mitomycin influences Lysine-specific demethylase 4C remains unclear, the shared targeting of SQ20B by multiple entities suggests a potential role in the regulation of this enzyme. The evidence points to SQ20B as a downstream target of mitomycin through a series of enzymatic interactions, though the precise molecular mechanism underlying this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
